Heat @chicken broth{1%quart} in a #stockpot over medium-low heat until warmed, ~{3-5%minutes}.

Heat @butter{1%tablespoon} and @olive oil{1%tablespoon} in a large, #heavy-bottomed pan{} until butter melts. Add @onion{0.5%medium}(minced) and sauté until translucent, about ~{2%minutes}. Stir in @Arborio rice{1.25%cups} until coated, then cook, stirring constantly, until fragrant, about ~{1%minute}.

Pour @white wine{0.5%cup} into rice mixture; cook and stir until liquid is absorbed, about ~{5%minutes}. Add one ladle hot broth and cook, stirring constantly, until broth is absorbed. Continue adding and stirring in one ladle broth at a time until rice is tender but firm to the bite, ~{20-30%minutes}. If you run out of broth before rice is cooked, finish cooking with @hot water{0.25%cup}.

Stir in @grated Parmesan cheese{0.33%cup}, remaining @butter{2%tablespoons}, @white truffle oil{2%tablespoons}, and @milk{1%teaspoon} until fully incorporated, then season with @fresh parsley{2%tablespoons}(chopped), @salt{to taste}, and @ground black pepper{to taste}. Serve immediately.